tion=\"row\" >`"],[1919,"`<Flex justifyContent=\"center\">`"],[1871,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[493,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[1490,"`align` centers the parts as well as the text, so a `Tag` eyebrow stays centered too."],[1056,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1238,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[354,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[247,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[1057,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1239,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[249,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1059,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1569,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1240,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[353,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[957,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[248,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1058,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[351,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[955,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[954,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value"],[350,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[956,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[352,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[1863,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[122,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[1674,"`categoryColors` maps individual category values to palette color indices, overriding\nthe series color for just those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[233,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[303,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[321,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[299,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[314,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1611,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[1831,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[991,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[582,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[585,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[581,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[583,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[584,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[586,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1287,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[380,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[413,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[901,"`Enter/Space`"],[455,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[676,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[422,"`Escape`"],[828,"`Escape`"],[903,"`Escape`"],[1616,"`Escape`"],[492,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[1900,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[590,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[1938,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, i